 6. 🏛️ Thune&#x27;s post-election test 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Photo: Eric Lee/Bloomberg via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Sen. Dave McCormick (R-Pa.) last night called for a delay in tomorrow's Senate GOP leadership elections, injecting a surprise note of uncertainty into what had been a largely foregone conclusion before Republicans' devastating midterm defeat, Axios' Hans Nichols writes .

 Why it matters: No one has officially challenged Majority Leader John Thune (R-S.D.). But the push to delay — also backed by Sen. Ron Johnson (R-Wis.) — signals growing unease with plans to quickly reelect him. 🖼️ The big picture: President Trump clashed repeatedly with Thune over his resistance to eliminating the filibuster and the Senate's failure to pass parts of his agenda, like the SAVE America Act.

 Trump renewed his criticism after the midterms, blaming the Senate in part for Republicans' election losses. Read McCormick's post ... Get Axios Hill Leaders , our weeknight newsletter from the Capitol. 

 
 
