 7. 🎤 Axios interview: AI&#x27;s &quot;terrible&quot; marketing 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Axios Visuals. Photo: Ben Gibbs/Office of Eric and Wendy Schmidt

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Former Google CEO Eric Schmidt tells Axios' Madison Mills that he remains staunchly bullish on an industry facing rising social pushback, saying data centers can occupy America's "empty spaces" and predicting a near-term revolution in AI-assisted research.

 In a wide-ranging interview following his appointment to lead Caltech's board of trustees, Schmidt acknowledged the industry does a "terrible" job marketing itself to voters. Yet, looking from his new perch at what he calls the "crown jewel of nerddom," he sees an unstoppable wave of AI-augmented scientists poised to dominate the future workforce. "We talk about all the negatives without talking the positives, and people are much more likely to index their minds on the negatives," he says. 

