 8. 🍗 1 for the road: &#x27;27 food trends 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The rotisserie chicken at Chez Poulet in Chicago comes with chicken skin jus and a variety of sauce options, including garlic toum, salsa macha and French chimichurri. Photo: Kim Kovacik for The Infatuation As beef prices soar, chicken is the rising star of date night, according to a dining trends forecast from The Infatuation .

 Trendy restaurants are serving up their takes on the classic roast bird with unexpected sides, sauces and seasonings, Axios' Erica Pandey writes. 🌴 What else is trending: Miami's hot spots! For years, Miami was a secondary location for buzzy restaurants like Carbone and Cote . But now the city is exporting its own.

 Pura Vida , the Miami-born cafe and juice bar, is everywhere, including New York, D.C., Massachusetts and California. Skinny Louie , a smashburger spot, has also made the jump to New York City. Kyu , an upscale pan-Asian spot, started in Miami and has spread to L.A., Vegas and New York City. 👑 The Infatuation has also crowned its best new restaurants of 2026, which include D.C.'s Rye Bunny and Boulder's Casa Juani .

